WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:27.486 --> 00:00:28.779
I don't understand.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.280
Every time I go
through my hell loop,

00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:32.574
I keep making
the same mistakes.

00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:35.827
Well, that's because you're
avoiding your guilt, Reese.

00:00:35.911 --> 00:00:37.246
You need to confront it.

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:38.789
You all do.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:39.748
I don't know.

00:00:39.831 --> 00:00:41.917
I'm telling you,
no matter how hard I try,

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.586
it feels like I'm destined
to make the wrong choice.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.256
Ah, the old fate
versus free will debate.

00:00:47.339 --> 00:00:48.382
My favourite.

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:50.342
But you see,
fate is just a result

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:52.052
of the choices
that you make.

00:00:53.762 --> 00:00:56.223
Do you really think
it's possible to change?

00:00:56.306 --> 00:00:57.140
Of course.

00:00:57.224 --> 00:00:58.350
I mean, look at me.

00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:01.061
For millennia,
I was down here,

00:01:01.144 --> 00:01:04.273
stuck in my own
hell loop of sorts,

00:01:04.356 --> 00:01:05.858
thinking I deserve
to be in charge

00:01:05.941 --> 00:01:06.984
of people's punishment.

00:01:07.651 --> 00:01:08.694
And then even when I left,

00:01:08.777 --> 00:01:11.655
I found myself
in a cycle of selfishness

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:15.367
and violence,
debauchery, sex.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.077
Yeah, I mean, clearly,
it wasn't all bad,

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.912
but the point is that,

00:01:18.996 --> 00:01:21.498
with the right guidance
and the right help,

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.625
I was able to change,

00:01:23.709 --> 00:01:24.793
to grow,

00:01:24.877 --> 00:01:27.796
to find true
meaning in life.

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.133
I wish I could just…

00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:34.052
take it all back,

00:01:34.887 --> 00:01:36.513
everything
that I did on Earth.

00:01:37.389 --> 00:01:39.975
I hear you.
I felt that way, too.

00:01:40.684 --> 00:01:42.311
I wished I could do
everything differently,

00:01:42.394 --> 00:01:45.314
but then I wouldn't
be the devil I am right now

00:01:45.397 --> 00:01:48.358
sitting across from you
right here, would I?

00:01:48.442 --> 00:01:49.401
I don't know.

00:01:49.484 --> 00:01:51.403
Maybe I'm just a lost cause.

00:01:51.486 --> 00:01:52.613
Nonsense, Reese.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:54.907
And certainly
not on my watch.

00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:57.576
Because if the devil
can be redeemed

00:01:58.619 --> 00:01:59.870
then anyone can.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:03.332
And if you can't,

00:02:03.415 --> 00:02:05.167
I can just shoot you
in the face,

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.627
put you out
of your misery, no?

00:02:08.504 --> 00:02:12.341
No, Vincent, nobody will be
shooting anyone in the face.

00:02:13.509 --> 00:02:16.678
Clearly, you're going
to need a little more time.

00:02:18.013 --> 00:02:19.014
Ah!

00:02:19.097 --> 00:02:20.974
That'll be the doughnuts.

00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:23.435
And the pastries
for you, Vincent.

00:02:23.519 --> 00:02:24.645
Ah, c'est bon.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:34.154
Hello, Detective.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.954
I thought
you could use a partner.

